WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950
Cape Town, January 2018.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.110
A city of just over 4 million people.

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.850
The warning: in April, the taps in its
neighbourhoods could be turned off.

4
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.350
The city called it Day Zero.

5
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.990
What pushed a major city to the edge?

6
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.110
Burst pipes?

7
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.250
Polluted water?

8
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.650
A neighbouring country taking its water?

9
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.570
And how did it pull back?

10
00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.850
In this mission, you'll tell physical
water scarcity from economic scarcity,

11
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.850
and map both.

12
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.790
Then you'll meet the stakeholders, from
the national government to farmers and

13
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.650
households, and judge who did what.

14
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.790
Your mission: explain what
pushed Cape Town to the edge,

15
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.520
and how it pulled back.
